OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app
targets list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,
misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real,
compiled canonical admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the
sibling P7 admin pages (ApiPlayground, AuditLog, DiskForecast, SchemaDrift,
FleetTelemetryCoverage, LiveSignalInspector, TeslaOrders, Users) ship and which `Sources`
already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/
Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same reconciliation every sibling
admin-page log (AuditLog / DiskForecast / SchemaDrift) recorded; it is the only deviation
from the literal prompt path. An Xcode runner IS available (Xcode 26.5), so the gate is
NOT BLOCKED on a missing runner.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the admin sub-path `/admin/feedback`. Following the
sibling AuditLog/SchemaDrift pattern, a dedicated `.feedbackQueue` AppRoute case is added
(pathSegment `feedback`, System group, icon `exclamationmark.bubble.fill`),
`AppRouteParser` aliases `/admin/feedback` -> `.feedbackQueue`, and
`FeedbackQueueRouteRegistration` hosts `FeedbackQueuePage` on it, chained into
`\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift after IngestXRay. So the page is reachable via the
System-group sidebar entry and any `/admin/feedback` deep link. (Navigation registration
is an allowed file per the prompt.)

