POST-REVIEW HARDENING (code-review agent pass — 3 correctness fixes applied + 1 cosmetic noted)
================================================================================
An automated code-review pass against the web source + the Go backend
(internal/api/adminfeedback/handler.go) surfaced 3 genuine correctness/parity defects,
each FIXED IN MY OWN FILES (covenant #2), re-formatted + re-linted (0/0), re-run through
the harness (39 checks), and rebuilt green on macOS + iOS:

  FIX-1 (High, parity + info-exposure): the Reporter cell mirrored neither the web
  `UserCell` priority nor its single-line shape — it showed the opaque subject before the
  email, the full email instead of the local-part, AND rendered `submitter_ip` as a
  secondary line (the web cell is only handed {id, email} with showEmail=false, so it can
  never display the IP). Replaced `reporterName`/`reporterSecondary`+TSUserCell with
  `reporterCell` + `reporterDisplay` = email-local-part -> subject -> nil; nil renders the
  localized "avatar.unknown". Avatar + single line, IP never surfaced. (Table.swift)

  FIX-2 (Medium, behavior): a failed inline PATCH set state=.error, wiping the loaded
  queue + the admin's typed URL. The web mutation error is an independent toast that
  leaves the list query intact. `applyUpdate` now records `updateError` (surfaced as a
  dismissible TSAlertBanner keyed "toast.feedback.update.error") and keeps the loaded list.
  (FeedbackQueuePageModel.swift + FeedbackQueuePage.swift)

  FIX-3 (Medium, wire contract): `FeedbackUpdate.jsonBody: [String:String]` emitted
  `"forward_to_github":"true"` (a JSON string), but the backend struct is `ForwardToGitHub
  bool` decoded under `DisallowUnknownFields()` -> a JSON string 400s. Replaced with
  `FeedbackUpdate: Encodable` (snake_case CodingKeys + encodeIfPresent) so the field
  serializes as a JSON boolean `true` and only set fields are emitted. (Models.swift)

  NOTED (cosmetic, NOT changed): FeedbackQueueFormat.prettyJSON uses [.prettyPrinted,
  .sortedKeys] so recent_errors object keys render alphabetized vs the web's source order.
  Kept INTENTIONALLY — JSONSerialization cannot preserve source order anyway, and
  .sortedKeys yields deterministic output matching the sibling AuditLogFormat.prettyJSON.

All other reviewed areas (pagination math, filter->query snake_case, badge tone/label maps,
Save enable/disable, Forward visibility, list loading/empty/error/loaded routing) were
confirmed correct with no changes needed.


